From: Armada contributors <noreply@armadaos.dev>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: eliza: add CPU OPPs for L3 scaling

Without CPU interconnect requests, EPSS L3 falls to its lowest performance
state when interconnect synchronization releases the initial bandwidth
votes.

Add CPU interconnect paths and shared OPP tables to scale L3 with CPU
frequency. Derive the bandwidths from the downstream memlat tables and
CPU frequency LUTs on the Retroid Pocket Duo.

---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/eliza.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/eliza.dtsi
@@ -50,6 +50,10 @@
 
 			qcom,freq-domain = <&cpufreq_hw 0>;
 
+			operating-points-v2 = <&cpu0_opp_table>;
+			interconnects = <&epss_l3 MASTER_EPSS_L3_APPS
+					 &epss_l3 SLAVE_EPSS_L3_SHARED>;
+
 			l2_0: l2-cache {
 				compatible = "cache";
 				cache-level = <2>;
@@ -80,6 +84,10 @@
 			dynamic-power-coefficient = <100>;
 
 			qcom,freq-domain = <&cpufreq_hw 0>;
+
+			operating-points-v2 = <&cpu0_opp_table>;
+			interconnects = <&epss_l3 MASTER_EPSS_L3_APPS
+					 &epss_l3 SLAVE_EPSS_L3_SHARED>;
 		};
 
 		cpu2: cpu@200 {
@@ -98,6 +106,10 @@
